  "notes": "Dark IDE-style tool. The canvas uses a dotted grid; each pipeline (Traces amber, Metrics sky blue, Logs green) is a dashed-outline frame with a solid colored tab label and icon. Nodes are 146x97 rounded cards with a violet (#8b5cf6) title strip for receivers/exporters and blue for processors, a grey body with a line icon (download for receiver, chip for processor, upload for exporter), joined by thin straight arrows. Selecting a node live highlights its YAML line and turns the editor header into a breadcrumb path ('receivers > otlp') — not in capture. Validation dropdown (closed in capture) opens a rich popover choosing Browser-only vs distribution-specific validation with expandable distro cards (Core, Contrib, AWS, Splunk). Share popover includes a URL field, README badge, PNG preview of the visualization and Download YAML/Image buttons. Indigo (#6366f1) used for active/primary controls (validation button, lock toggle, Share)."
